Re-ran the pay production gate loop ~10 hours after the morning packet
landed. Result is byte-identical: runtime_probe_checkout_status=401,
shared_health_contract_shape=legacy_or_unknown, bundle_status=
BLOCKED_PRECHECK, all 8 unmet signals unchanged.

The duplicated reading is itself the proof that the lock is *not*
transient — owner still has not bound TEAM2_PAY_GATE_API_KEY nor
deployed the new pay /health shared contract. Logged the second run
in the existing TEAM1_OWNER_PING packet so the next escalation has
two timestamped data points. No code touched, no key fabricated, no
pay deploy attempted.

Trust-state regenerated as a side-effect of the build-commit pin.
Module-1 counts hold: verified=13, declared=5 — invoice.iai.one drop
remains sticky.
